{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QKd8K491C2tNrBMjKiHwZH","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nslug: pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone\nstatus: draft\ncreated_at: 2026-11-23\ncompleted_at:\nsupersedes:\ndepends_on: \nremediates:\npriority: 2\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: bugfix\nsurface: standard\ndelivers: capability:validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nMake the engine's own Git reads during `pose validate` and `pose check`, such as the provenance status of `validate`, never rewrite `.git/index` or take index locks in the validated checkout.\n\n### Business value\nIn Harne8 the governance read view of `instance-health-composite` failed intermittently with `review inputs changed during operation: .git` because concurrent reads refreshed the index stat cache. The Harne8 bugfix `harne8-validation-reads-leave-root-index-alone` fixed the instance's own scripts and left this engine part as its follow-up F1.\n\n### Constraints\nReads keep their results. Stale stat caches may cost time, never correctness.\n\n### Non-goals\nChanging which files are compared.\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: Every status, diff and ls-files read the engine makes for validation provenance, material cleanliness and readiness checks shall run with optional locks disabled, and a diff against the work tree shall read the index without being able to write it, so none rewrites `.git/index` or takes its lock (D1).\n- R2: A regression test shall run those reads over a checkout with a stale stat cache and prove `.git/index` byte-identical afterwards.\n- R3: A concurrency test shall run those reads together on one checkout while a reader watches `.git/index` and its lock, and see neither change (D2).\n\n### Non-functional\nExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n\n### Security\nNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n\n### Compatibility\nRecords and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n`pose-mcp`: the engine's Git command constructor (`gitCommandContext`), work-tree read helpers (`git_worktree_reads.go`), and the work-tree diffs of `check` (ready transitions), `validate` scope selection, `report` and the review history ledger.\n\n### Artifacts\n- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_other.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\n\n### Delivery targets\n- capability:validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\n\n### Accepted limits\n- L1: A Git command the engine runs through another constructor, or a tool a validation step runs, can still refresh the index. Accepted because every engine read goes through `gitCommandContext`, and what a step runs is the project's command, which the Harne8 bugfix of its own scripts already covers.\n- L2: Outside Linux there is no anonymous memory file, so a diff reads a private copy of the index in a temporary directory, which a dry run there would create. Accepted because the copy keeps the checkout's index untouched, which is the defect, and the dry-run test that forbids any file runs on Linux only.\n\n### API/contract changes\nNone: the reads answer as before; only where their stat refresh is written changes.\n\n### Data/storage changes\nNone.\n\n### Technical risks\nIf Git stopped skipping a failed refresh lock silently, the diff would fail instead of answering; the equivalence test would show it.\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Planning\n- [x] Confirm the requirements against the current engine before starting.\n\n### Implementation\n- [x] Implement each requirement with a test that fails before it.\n\n### Validation\n- [ ] `pose validate --carry` and `pose check --strict`.\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Basis: R1\nR1 as drafted asked for `diff.autoRefreshIndex=false`. Measured on a stale stat cache, `git diff --name-only HEAD` rewrites the index even with `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, and with `diff.autoRefreshIndex=false` it lists a file whose stat alone changed, which breaks the constraint that reads keep their results. So every engine Git command carries `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` (enough for `git status`), and a diff against the work tree runs unchanged but reads the index through `GIT_INDEX_FILE=/proc/self/fd/N`, an anonymous memory file (`memfd`) holding the index's bytes. Git resolves that link to `/memfd:pose-index/none (deleted)`, cannot create its lock beside it (the directory does not exist, for any user), and skips the refresh write silently, so the answer is the plain diff's and nothing is written. Two earlier versions were refused: a private copy of the index in a temporary file, by the full suite (a dry run creates no file, `TestUpdatePreviewHasNoPhysicalMutationEvents`); and answers rebuilt from `git status`, by review round 1, which found five states they got wrong (submodules ignored by configuration, conflicts, symlinks, a POSE root below the repository top). Outside Linux the copy is used (L2).\n\n### Decision D2\n- Basis: R3\nR3 as drafted ran `validate` and `check --strict` together. The property they broke is that a reader saw `.git` change under it; the test runs the reads those commands make, concurrently, while a reader watches `.git/index` and `index.lock`, which shows the property directly and runs in under a second instead of a full validation.\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nEach requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n\n### Execution log\n- 2026-11-26: `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` in `gitCommandContext`; the work-tree diffs of the ready-transition read, scope selection, `report --since` and the review history ledger read `git status` (`WorktreeChanges`, `WorktreeChangedNames`). `TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone`, `TestConcurrentValidationReadsNeverChangeTheIndex` and `TestWorktreeReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone` fail with each guard mutated out (the optional-locks setting, each caller's `git diff` restored, the content comparison); the last also checks the answers equal `git diff` for a commit since the base, a modified, a deleted and a staged-new file. A first private-index version was refused by the full suite (D1).\n- 2026-11-26: review round 1 (rrn-b249b5d958a5d8ff) requested changes with N1–N9: the status-based answers differed from `git diff` for a submodule ignored by `.gitmodules`, a submodule with uncommitted content, symlinks and a directory replaced by a file, unmerged entries, a POSE root below the repository top, intent-to-add, staged-then-reverted changes and a range base. They were withdrawn: the callers run their original `git diff` again, reading the index through a `memfd` (D1). `TestReadOnlyIndexDiffAnswersAsThePlainDiff` builds those states and requires each read to answer byte for byte as the plain diff, leave `.git/index` identical and leave no lock; it also runs the review history ledger's diff (N9). Each guard fails its test mutated out.\n\n### Results summary\nThe full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone, test:TestReadOnlyIndexDiffAnswersAsThePlainDiff\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestConcurrentValidationReadsNeverChangeTheIndex\n\n### Known gaps\nNone.\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\nThe engine's Git reads during `validate`, `check` and `report` no longer rewrite `.git/index` or take its lock, and keep their answers.\n\n### Files and modules changed\n`pose-mcp` Git command construction and the work-tree diffs of check, validate scope, report and the review history ledger.\n\n### Validation executed\n`go test ./...` in `pose-mcp`; `pose check --strict`; `pose validate --carry --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json`.\n\n### Residual risks\nL1 and L2 above.\n\n### Follow-ups\nNone.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"f6c4a019-9300-480d-b4e3-4828c57db630","timestamp":"2026-11-26T15:26:23.003Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"---\nslug: pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone\nstatus: draft\ncreated_at: 2026-11-23\ncompleted_at:\nsupersedes:\ndepends_on: \nremediates:\npriority: 2\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: bugfix\nsurface: standard\ndelivers: capability:validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nMake the engine's own Git reads during `pose validate` and `pose check`, such as the provenance status of `validate`, never rewrite `.git/index` or take index locks in the validated checkout.\n\n### Business value\nIn Harne8 the governance read view of `instance-health-composite` failed intermittently with `review inputs changed during operation: .git` because concurrent reads refreshed the index stat cache. The Harne8 bugfix `harne8-validation-reads-leave-root-index-alone` fixed the instance's own scripts and left this engine part as its follow-up F1.\n\n### Constraints\nReads keep their results. Stale stat caches may cost time, never correctness.\n\n### Non-goals\nChanging which files are compared.\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: Every status, diff and ls-files read the engine makes for validation provenance, material cleanliness and readiness checks shall run with optional locks disabled, and a diff against the work tree shall read the index without being able to write it, so none rewrites `.git/index` or takes its lock (D1).\n- R2: A regression test shall run those reads over a checkout with a stale stat cache and prove `.git/index` byte-identical afterwards.\n- R3: A concurrency test shall run those reads together on one checkout while a reader watches `.git/index` and its lock, and see neither change (D2).\n\n### Non-functional\nExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n\n### Security\nNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n\n### Compatibility\nRecords and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n`pose-mcp`: the engine's Git command constructor (`gitCommandContext`), work-tree read helpers (`git_worktree_reads.go`), and the work-tree diffs of `check` (ready transitions), `validate` scope selection, `report` and the review history ledger.\n\n### Artifacts\n- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_other.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\n\n### Delivery targets\n- capability:validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\n\n### Accepted limits\n- L1: A Git command the engine runs through another constructor, or a tool a validation step runs, can still refresh the index. Accepted because every engine read goes through `gitCommandContext`, and what a step runs is the project's command, which the Harne8 bugfix of its own scripts already covers.\n- L2: Outside Linux there is no anonymous memory file, so a diff reads a private copy of the index in a temporary directory, which a dry run there would create. Accepted because the copy keeps the checkout's index untouched, which is the defect, and the dry-run test that forbids any file runs on Linux only.\n\n### API/contract changes\nNone: the reads answer as before; only where their stat refresh is written changes.\n\n### Data/storage changes\nNone.\n\n### Technical risks\nIf Git stopped skipping a failed refresh lock silently, the diff would fail instead of answering; the equivalence test would show it.\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Planning\n- [x] Confirm the requirements against the current engine before starting.\n\n### Implementation\n- [x] Implement each requirement with a test that fails before it.\n\n### Validation\n- [ ] `pose validate --carry` and `pose check --strict`.\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Basis: R1\nR1 as drafted asked for `diff.autoRefreshIndex=false`. Measured on a stale stat cache, `git diff --name-only HEAD` rewrites the index even with `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, and with `diff.autoRefreshIndex=false` it lists a file whose stat alone changed, which breaks the constraint that reads keep their results. So every engine Git command carries `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` (enough for `git status`), and a diff against the work tree runs unchanged but reads the index through `GIT_INDEX_FILE=/proc/self/fd/N`, an anonymous memory file (`memfd`) holding the index's bytes. Git resolves that link to `/memfd:pose-index/none (deleted)`, cannot create its lock beside it (the directory does not exist, for any user), and skips the refresh write silently, so the answer is the plain diff's and nothing is written. Two earlier versions were refused: a private copy of the index in a temporary file, by the full suite (a dry run creates no file, `TestUpdatePreviewHasNoPhysicalMutationEvents`); and answers rebuilt from `git status`, by review round 1, which found five states they got wrong (submodules ignored by configuration, conflicts, symlinks, a POSE root below the repository top). Outside Linux the copy is used (L2).\n\n### Decision D2\n- Basis: R3\nR3 as drafted ran `validate` and `check --strict` together. The property they broke is that a reader saw `.git` change under it; the test runs the reads those commands make, concurrently, while a reader watches `.git/index` and `index.lock`, which shows the property directly and runs in under a second instead of a full validation.\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nEach requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n\n### Execution log\n- 2026-11-26: `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` in `gitCommandContext`; the work-tree diffs of the ready-transition read, scope selection, `report --since` and the review history ledger read `git status` (`WorktreeChanges`, `WorktreeChangedNames`). `TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone`, `TestConcurrentValidationReadsNeverChangeTheIndex` and `TestWorktreeReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone` fail with each guard mutated out (the optional-locks setting, each caller's `git diff` restored, the content comparison); the last also checks the answers equal `git diff` for a commit since the base, a modified, a deleted and a staged-new file. A first private-index version was refused by the full suite (D1).\n- 2026-11-26: review round 1 (rrn-b249b5d958a5d8ff) requested changes with N1–N9: the status-based answers differed from `git diff` for a submodule ignored by `.gitmodules`, a submodule with uncommitted content, symlinks and a directory replaced by a file, unmerged entries, a POSE root below the repository top, intent-to-add, staged-then-reverted changes and a range base. They were withdrawn: the callers run their original `git diff` again, reading the index through a `memfd` (D1). `TestReadOnlyIndexDiffAnswersAsThePlainDiff` builds those states and requires each read to answer byte for byte as the plain diff, leave `.git/index` identical and leave no lock; it also runs the review history ledger's diff (N9). Each guard fails its test mutated out.\n\n### Results summary\nThe full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone, test:TestReadOnlyIndexDiffAnswersAsThePlainDiff\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestConcurrentValidationReadsNeverChangeTheIndex\n\n### Known gaps\nNone.\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\nThe engine's Git reads during `validate`, `check` and `report` no longer rewrite `.git/index` or take its lock, and keep their answers.\n\n### Files and modules changed\n`pose-mcp` Git command construction and the work-tree diffs of check, validate scope, report and the review history ledger.\n\n### Validation executed\n`go test ./...` in `pose-mcp`; `pose check --strict`; `pose validate --carry --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json`.\n\n### Residual risks\nL1 and L2 above.\n\n### Follow-ups\nNone.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QKd8K491C2tNrBMjKiHwZH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WuwumZBuZ3JCxRwPabg2fC","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\nindex 991e096c..cbe26ac8 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\n@@ -1131,7 +1131,16 @@ func (checker *nativeChecker) readyTransitionCandidates() []string {\n \t\t{\"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"HEAD\", \"--\", \".pose/specs\"},\n \t\t{\"ls-files\", \"--others\", \"--exclude-standard\", \"--\", \".pose/specs\"},\n \t} {\n-\t\toutput, err := pose.RawHistoryGit(checker.root, command...).Output()\n+\t\t// The diff reads the index without writing it (spec\n+\t\t// pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1).\n+\t\tcmd := pose.RawHistoryGit(checker.root, command...)\n+\t\tdone, err := pose.ReadOnlyIndex(cmd, checker.root)\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\tdone()\n+\t\t\tcontinue\n+\t\t}\n+\t\toutput, err := cmd.Output()\n+\t\tdone()\n \t\tif err != nil {\n \t\t\tcontinue\n \t\t}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\nindex 0ed37869..8f26fbd0 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n@@ -298,7 +298,9 @@ func reportChangedFiles(root, since string) []string {\n \t} else {\n \t\targs = append(args, \"status\", \"--porcelain=v1\")\n \t}\n-\toutput, err := posemodel.RawGit(args...).Output()\n+\t// The diff reads the index without writing it (spec\n+\t// pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1).\n+\toutput, err := posemodel.RawGitDiffReadOnly(root, args...)\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn nil\n \t}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..663b28a7\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,121 @@\n+package cli\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"bytes\"\n+\t\"os\"\n+\t\"os/exec\"\n+\t\"path/filepath\"\n+\t\"sync\"\n+\t\"testing\"\n+\t\"time\"\n+)\n+\n+// staleIndexRepo is a repository whose index holds a stale stat cache for a\n+// file whose content did not change, so any read that refreshes the index\n+// would write it back.\n+func staleIndexRepo(t *testing.T) (string, []byte) {\n+\tt.Helper()\n+\troot := t.TempDir()\n+\tgit := func(args ...string) {\n+\t\tt.Helper()\n+\t\tcmd := exec.Command(\"git\", append([]string{\"-C\", root, \"-c\", \"user.name=t\", \"-c\", \"user.email=t@t\"}, args...)...)\n+\t\tif out, err := cmd.CombinedOutput(); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"git %v: %v %s\", args, err, out)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tgit(\"init\", \"-q\")\n+\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Join(root, \".pose\", \"specs\"), 0o755); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, f := range []string{\"a.txt\", \".pose/specs/2026-11-26-alpha.md\"} {\n+\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, f), []byte(\"x\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tgit(\"add\", \"-A\")\n+\tgit(\"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"init\")\n+\tlater := time.Now().Add(2 * time.Second)\n+\tfor _, f := range []string{\"a.txt\", \".pose/specs/2026-11-26-alpha.md\"} {\n+\t\tif err := os.Chtimes(filepath.Join(root, f), later, later); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tindex, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\"))\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\treturn root, index\n+}\n+\n+// Spec pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1, R2: the reads validate,\n+// check and report make leave a stale index byte-identical, and still answer\n+// that nothing changed.\n+func TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot, before := staleIndexRepo(t)\n+\tif !materialWorktreeClean(root) {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"a stat-only change made the work tree dirty\")\n+\t}\n+\tsel, err := computeChangedScopeWith(root, \"HEAD\", \"\", nil, scopeMetadata{})\n+\tif err != nil || len(sel.Changed) != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the scope diff against the work tree: %v %v\", sel.Changed, err)\n+\t}\n+\tif files := reportChangedFiles(root, \"HEAD\"); len(files) != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"report listed a stat-only change: %v\", files)\n+\t}\n+\tif got := (&nativeChecker{root: root}).readyTransitionCandidates(); len(got) != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the ready transition read listed a stat-only change: %v\", got)\n+\t}\n+\tafter, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\"))\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tif !bytes.Equal(before, after) {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"a validation read rewrote .git/index\")\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// Spec pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R3: while those reads run\n+// concurrently, a reader watching .git/index never sees it change.\n+func TestConcurrentValidationReadsNeverChangeTheIndex(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot, before := staleIndexRepo(t)\n+\tstop := make(chan struct{})\n+\tvar wg sync.WaitGroup\n+\tfor i := 0; i < 4; i++ {\n+\t\twg.Add(1)\n+\t\tgo func() {\n+\t\t\tdefer wg.Done()\n+\t\t\tfor j := 0; j < 5; j++ {\n+\t\t\t\tmaterialWorktreeClean(root)\n+\t\t\t\t_, _ = computeChangedScopeWith(root, \"HEAD\", \"\", nil, scopeMetadata{})\n+\t\t\t\treportChangedFiles(root, \"HEAD\")\n+\t\t\t\t(&nativeChecker{root: root}).readyTransitionCandidates()\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t}()\n+\t}\n+\tchanged := make(chan string, 1)\n+\tgo func() {\n+\t\tfor {\n+\t\t\tselect {\n+\t\t\tcase <-stop:\n+\t\t\t\treturn\n+\t\t\tdefault:\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tnow, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\"))\n+\t\t\tif err == nil && !bytes.Equal(before, now) {\n+\t\t\t\tchanged <- \"the index changed while validation reads ran\"\n+\t\t\t\treturn\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tif _, err := os.Lstat(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index.lock\")); err == nil {\n+\t\t\t\tchanged <- \"a validation read took the index lock\"\n+\t\t\t\treturn\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t}\n+\t}()\n+\twg.Wait()\n+\tclose(stop)\n+\tselect {\n+\tcase why := <-changed:\n+\t\tt.Fatal(why)\n+\tdefault:\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\nindex 2f0ad346..d4b2c6e2 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n@@ -102,7 +102,9 @@ func computeChangedScopeWith(root, base, head string, modules []validationModule\n \t\tgitArgs = append(gitArgs, head)\n \t}\n \tgitArgs = append(gitArgs, \"--\")\n-\tout, err := posemodel.RawGit(gitArgs...).Output()\n+\t// The diff reads the index without writing it (spec\n+\t// pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1).\n+\tout, err := posemodel.RawGitDiffReadOnly(root, gitArgs...)\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn sel, fmt.Errorf(\"git diff %s failed (revision unknown?)\", sel.rangeLabel())\n \t}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go\nindex b95cd8fb..e0bc034f 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go\n@@ -656,7 +656,10 @@ func gitCommandContext(ctx context.Context, args ...string) *exec.Cmd {\n \t\t\tenv = append(env, kv)\n \t\t}\n \t}\n-\tcmd.Env = append(env, \"GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS=1\", \"GIT_GRAFT_FILE=\"+os.DevNull)\n+\t// An engine read never takes the optional index lock nor rewrites the\n+\t// index's stat cache: a concurrent reader would see .git change under\n+\t// it (spec pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1).\n+\tcmd.Env = append(env, \"GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS=1\", \"GIT_GRAFT_FILE=\"+os.DevNull, \"GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0\")\n \treturn cmd\n }\n \ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..a9dbd243\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@\n+package pose\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"fmt\"\n+\t\"os/exec\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+)\n+\n+// Spec pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1, D1: `git diff` against\n+// the work tree refreshes the index's stat cache and writes it back even with\n+// GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0, and diff.autoRefreshIndex=false would change its\n+// answer (a file whose stat alone changed would be listed). So the diff runs\n+// as it is, but reads the index through a descriptor whose lock Git cannot\n+// create: it refreshes in memory, cannot write, and skips the write silently\n+// (refresh_index_quietly), so its answer is the plain diff's and nothing is\n+// written anywhere. Where that is not available, it reads a private copy.\n+\n+// diffIndexLimit bounds the index one read loads.\n+const diffIndexLimit = 512 << 20\n+\n+// ReadOnlyIndex prepares cmd, a git command reading the repository at root,\n+// to read root's index without being able to write it. The returned function\n+// releases what it holds; call it after the command ends.\n+func ReadOnlyIndex(cmd *exec.Cmd, root string) (func(), error) {\n+\tout, err := RawGit(\"-C\", root, \"rev-parse\", \"--path-format=absolute\", \"--git-path\", \"index\").Output()\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s cannot be located: %w\", root, err)\n+\t}\n+\traw, err := readBoundedRegular(strings.TrimSuffix(string(out), \"\\n\"), diffIndexLimit)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s cannot be read: %w\", root, err)\n+\t}\n+\treturn readOnlyIndexFor(cmd, raw)\n+}\n+\n+// RawGitDiffReadOnly runs RawGit(args...), a diff of the repository at root,\n+// reading its index without writing it, and returns its standard output.\n+func RawGitDiffReadOnly(root string, args ...string) ([]byte, error) {\n+\tcmd := RawGit(args...)\n+\tdone, err := ReadOnlyIndex(cmd, root)\n+\tdefer done()\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn nil, err\n+\t}\n+\treturn cmd.Output()\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..05ef93ed\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@\n+//go:build linux\n+\n+package pose\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"fmt\"\n+\t\"os\"\n+\t\"os/exec\"\n+\n+\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n+)\n+\n+// readOnlyIndexFor hands raw to cmd as an anonymous memory file. Git\n+// resolves the link /proc/self/fd/N to \"/memfd:pose-index/none (deleted)\"\n+// and tries to create its lock next to it, in a directory that does not\n+// exist, so the lock fails for any user, root included, and the refresh is\n+// not written. No file is created.\n+func readOnlyIndexFor(cmd *exec.Cmd, raw []byte) (func(), error) {\n+\tfd, err := unix.MemfdCreate(\"pose-index/none\", unix.MFD_CLOEXEC)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: an in-memory index cannot be made: %w\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tf := os.NewFile(uintptr(fd), \"pose-index\")\n+\tif _, err := f.Write(raw); err != nil {\n+\t\tf.Close()\n+\t\treturn func() {}, err\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := f.Seek(0, 0); err != nil {\n+\t\tf.Close()\n+\t\treturn func() {}, err\n+\t}\n+\tcmd.ExtraFiles = append(cmd.ExtraFiles, f)\n+\tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Env, fmt.Sprintf(\"GIT_INDEX_FILE=/proc/self/fd/%d\", 2+len(cmd.ExtraFiles)))\n+\treturn func() { f.Close() }, nil\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_other.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_other.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..1b633784\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_other.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@\n+//go:build !linux\n+\n+package pose\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"os\"\n+\t\"os/exec\"\n+\t\"path/filepath\"\n+)\n+\n+// readOnlyIndexFor hands raw to cmd as a private copy: Git refreshes and may\n+// rewrite the copy, never the checkout's index.\n+func readOnlyIndexFor(cmd *exec.Cmd, raw []byte) (func(), error) {\n+\tdir, err := os.MkdirTemp(\"\", \"pose-index-*\")\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn func() {}, err\n+\t}\n+\tdone := func() { _ = os.RemoveAll(dir) }\n+\tpath := filepath.Join(dir, \"index\")\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(path, raw, 0o600); err != nil {\n+\t\tdone()\n+\t\treturn func() {}, err\n+\t}\n+\t// A split index would write a new shared index into .git.\n+\tcmd.Args = append([]string{cmd.Args[0], \"-c\", \"core.splitIndex=false\"}, cmd.Args[1:]...)\n+\tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Env, \"GIT_INDEX_FILE=\"+path)\n+\treturn done, nil\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..fbe9c788\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,142 @@\n+package pose\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"bytes\"\n+\t\"os\"\n+\t\"os/exec\"\n+\t\"path/filepath\"\n+\t\"testing\"\n+\t\"time\"\n+)\n+\n+// Spec pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1, R2: a diff that reads the\n+// index read-only answers exactly as the plain diff does, over the states\n+// review round 1 found a status-based reading got wrong, and leaves the index\n+// byte-identical where the plain diff rewrites it.\n+func TestReadOnlyIndexDiffAnswersAsThePlainDiff(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot := t.TempDir()\n+\trun := func(dir string, args ...string) string {\n+\t\tt.Helper()\n+\t\tcmd := exec.Command(\"git\", append([]string{\"-C\", dir, \"-c\", \"user.name=t\", \"-c\", \"user.email=t@t\", \"-c\", \"protocol.file.allow=always\"}, args...)...)\n+\t\tout, err := cmd.CombinedOutput()\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"git %v: %v %s\", args, err, out)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\treturn string(out)\n+\t}\n+\twrite := func(rel, body string) {\n+\t\tt.Helper()\n+\t\tp := filepath.Join(root, rel)\n+\t\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(p), 0o755); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(p, []byte(body), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\t// A submodule whose .gitmodules says ignore=all.\n+\tsub := t.TempDir()\n+\trun(sub, \"init\", \"-q\")\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(sub, \"s.txt\"), []byte(\"1\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\trun(sub, \"add\", \"s.txt\")\n+\trun(sub, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"s1\")\n+\trun(root, \"init\", \"-q\")\n+\tfor _, f := range []string{\"stat.txt\", \"mod.txt\", \"del.txt\", \"proj/back.txt\", \"dir/x.txt\", \"conflict.txt\"} {\n+\t\twrite(f, \"x\\n\")\n+\t}\n+\tif err := os.Symlink(\"target-missing\", filepath.Join(root, \"link\")); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\trun(root, \"add\", \"-A\")\n+\trun(root, \"submodule\", \"add\", \"-q\", sub, \"mod\")\n+\trun(root, \"config\", \"-f\", \".gitmodules\", \"submodule.mod.ignore\", \"all\")\n+\trun(root, \"add\", \".gitmodules\")\n+\trun(root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"base\")\n+\tbase := run(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\")[:40]\n+\t// A commit since the base: the gitlink moves, and a file changes and is\n+\t// changed back in the work tree.\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, \"mod\", \"s.txt\"), []byte(\"2\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\trun(filepath.Join(root, \"mod\"), \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-am\", \"s2\")\n+\twrite(\"proj/back.txt\", \"y\\n\")\n+\trun(root, \"add\", \"-A\")\n+\trun(root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"next\")\n+\twrite(\"proj/back.txt\", \"x\\n\")\n+\t// Work-tree states.\n+\twrite(\"mod.txt\", \"changed\\n\")\n+\tif err := os.Remove(filepath.Join(root, \"del.txt\")); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\twrite(\"staged.txt\", \"s\\n\")\n+\trun(root, \"add\", \"staged.txt\")\n+\twrite(\"ita.txt\", \"i\\n\")\n+\trun(root, \"add\", \"-N\", \"ita.txt\")\n+\twrite(\"conflict.txt\", \"staged then reverted\\n\")\n+\trun(root, \"add\", \"conflict.txt\")\n+\twrite(\"conflict.txt\", \"x\\n\")\n+\tif err := os.RemoveAll(filepath.Join(root, \"dir\")); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\twrite(\"dir\", \"now a file\\n\")\n+\tlater := time.Now().Add(2 * time.Second)\n+\tif err := os.Chtimes(filepath.Join(root, \"stat.txt\"), later, later); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\treads := [][]string{\n+\t\t{\"-C\", root, \"-c\", \"diff.ignoreSubmodules=none\", \"diff\", \"--ignore-submodules=none\", \"--name-only\", \"-z\", \"--no-renames\", base, \"--\"},\n+\t\t{\"-C\", root, \"diff\", \"HEAD\", \"--name-status\", \"--no-renames\", \"--diff-filter=MDT\", \"--\"},\n+\t\t{\"-C\", filepath.Join(root, \"proj\"), \"diff\", \"--name-only\", base},\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, args := range reads {\n+\t\tbefore, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\"))\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tgot, err := RawGitDiffReadOnly(root, args...)\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%v: %v\", args, err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tafter, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\"))\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif !bytes.Equal(before, after) {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%v rewrote .git/index\", args)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\twant, err := RawGit(args...).Output()\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif !bytes.Equal(got, want) {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%v answered %q, the plain diff %q\", args, got, want)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\t// Make the stat cache stale again for the next read.\n+\t\tlater = later.Add(2 * time.Second)\n+\t\tif err := os.Chtimes(filepath.Join(root, \"stat.txt\"), later, later); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\t// The review history ledger's own diff (review round 1, N9).\n+\tbefore, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\"))\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := reviewHistoryGit(root, \"diff\", \"HEAD\", \"--name-status\", \"--no-renames\", \"--diff-filter=MDT\", \"--\"); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tif after, _ := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\")); !bytes.Equal(before, after) {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"the review history diff rewrote .git/index\")\n+\t}\n+\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(filepath.Join(root, \".git\"))\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, e := range entries {\n+\t\tif filepath.Ext(e.Name()) == \".lock\" {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a read left %s\", e.Name())\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\nindex 8cd9edb4..15a1dae2 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n@@ -530,6 +530,15 @@ func reviewHistoryGit(root string, args ...string) ([]byte, error) {\n \tbase := gitCommand(append([]string{\"-C\", root}, args...)...)\n \tcmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, \"git\", base.Args[1:]...)\n \tcmd.Env = base.Env\n+\tif len(args) > 0 && args[0] == \"diff\" {\n+\t\t// A diff against the work tree reads the index without writing it\n+\t\t// (spec pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1).\n+\t\tdone, err := ReadOnlyIndex(cmd, root)\n+\t\tdefer done()\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"review history Git observation unavailable: %w\", err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n \tvar out reviewHistoryBuffer\n \tcmd.Stdout = &out\n \tif err := cmd.Run(); err != nil {","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"3ed345a1-e6eb-4887-ae5f-ed6e13a1b4a3","timestamp":"2026-11-26T15:26:23.006Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"diff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\nindex 991e096c..cbe26ac8 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\n@@ -1131,7 +1131,16 @@ func (checker *nativeChecker) readyTransitionCandidates() []string {\n \t\t{\"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"HEAD\", \"--\", \".pose/specs\"},\n \t\t{\"ls-files\", \"--others\", \"--exclude-standard\", \"--\", \".pose/specs\"},\n \t} {\n-\t\toutput, err := pose.RawHistoryGit(checker.root, command...).Output()\n+\t\t// The diff reads the index without writing it (spec\n+\t\t// pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1).\n+\t\tcmd := pose.RawHistoryGit(checker.root, command...)\n+\t\tdone, err := pose.ReadOnlyIndex(cmd, checker.root)\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\tdone()\n+\t\t\tcontinue\n+\t\t}\n+\t\toutput, err := cmd.Output()\n+\t\tdone()\n \t\tif err != nil {\n \t\t\tcontinue\n \t\t}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\nindex 0ed37869..8f26fbd0 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n@@ -298,7 +298,9 @@ func reportChangedFiles(root, since string) []string {\n \t} else {\n \t\targs = append(args, \"status\", \"--porcelain=v1\")\n \t}\n-\toutput, err := posemodel.RawGit(args...).Output()\n+\t// The diff reads the index without writing it (spec\n+\t// pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1).\n+\toutput, err := posemodel.RawGitDiffReadOnly(root, args...)\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn nil\n \t}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..663b28a7\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,121 @@\n+package cli\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"bytes\"\n+\t\"os\"\n+\t\"os/exec\"\n+\t\"path/filepath\"\n+\t\"sync\"\n+\t\"testing\"\n+\t\"time\"\n+)\n+\n+// staleIndexRepo is a repository whose index holds a stale stat cache for a\n+// file whose content did not change, so any read that refreshes the index\n+// would write it back.\n+func staleIndexRepo(t *testing.T) (string, []byte) {\n+\tt.Helper()\n+\troot := t.TempDir()\n+\tgit := func(args ...string) {\n+\t\tt.Helper()\n+\t\tcmd := exec.Command(\"git\", append([]string{\"-C\", root, \"-c\", \"user.name=t\", \"-c\", \"user.email=t@t\"}, args...)...)\n+\t\tif out, err := cmd.CombinedOutput(); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"git %v: %v %s\", args, err, out)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tgit(\"init\", \"-q\")\n+\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Join(root, \".pose\", \"specs\"), 0o755); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, f := range []string{\"a.txt\", \".pose/specs/2026-11-26-alpha.md\"} {\n+\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, f), []byte(\"x\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tgit(\"add\", \"-A\")\n+\tgit(\"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"init\")\n+\tlater := time.Now().Add(2 * time.Second)\n+\tfor _, f := range []string{\"a.txt\", \".pose/specs/2026-11-26-alpha.md\"} {\n+\t\tif err := os.Chtimes(filepath.Join(root, f), later, later); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tindex, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\"))\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\treturn root, index\n+}\n+\n+// Spec pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1, R2: the reads validate,\n+// check and report make leave a stale index byte-identical, and still answer\n+// that nothing changed.\n+func TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot, before := staleIndexRepo(t)\n+\tif !materialWorktreeClean(root) {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"a stat-only change made the work tree dirty\")\n+\t}\n+\tsel, err := computeChangedScopeWith(root, \"HEAD\", \"\", nil, scopeMetadata{})\n+\tif err != nil || len(sel.Changed) != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the scope diff against the work tree: %v %v\", sel.Changed, err)\n+\t}\n+\tif files := reportChangedFiles(root, \"HEAD\"); len(files) != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"report listed a stat-only change: %v\", files)\n+\t}\n+\tif got := (&nativeChecker{root: root}).readyTransitionCandidates(); len(got) != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the ready transition read listed a stat-only change: %v\", got)\n+\t}\n+\tafter, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\"))\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tif !bytes.Equal(before, after) {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"a validation read rewrote .git/index\")\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// Spec pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R3: while those reads run\n+// concurrently, a reader watching .git/index never sees it change.\n+func TestConcurrentValidationReadsNeverChangeTheIndex(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot, before := staleIndexRepo(t)\n+\tstop := make(chan struct{})\n+\tvar wg sync.WaitGroup\n+\tfor i := 0; i < 4; i++ {\n+\t\twg.Add(1)\n+\t\tgo func() {\n+\t\t\tdefer wg.Done()\n+\t\t\tfor j := 0; j < 5; j++ {\n+\t\t\t\tmaterialWorktreeClean(root)\n+\t\t\t\t_, _ = computeChangedScopeWith(root, \"HEAD\", \"\", nil, scopeMetadata{})\n+\t\t\t\treportChangedFiles(root, \"HEAD\")\n+\t\t\t\t(&nativeChecker{root: root}).readyTransitionCandidates()\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t}()\n+\t}\n+\tchanged := make(chan string, 1)\n+\tgo func() {\n+\t\tfor {\n+\t\t\tselect {\n+\t\t\tcase <-stop:\n+\t\t\t\treturn\n+\t\t\tdefault:\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tnow, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\"))\n+\t\t\tif err == nil && !bytes.Equal(before, now) {\n+\t\t\t\tchanged <- \"the index changed while validation reads ran\"\n+\t\t\t\treturn\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tif _, err := os.Lstat(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index.lock\")); err == nil {\n+\t\t\t\tchanged <- \"a validation read took the index lock\"\n+\t\t\t\treturn\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t}\n+\t}()\n+\twg.Wait()\n+\tclose(stop)\n+\tselect {\n+\tcase why := <-changed:\n+\t\tt.Fatal(why)\n+\tdefault:\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\nindex 2f0ad346..d4b2c6e2 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n@@ -102,7 +102,9 @@ func computeChangedScopeWith(root, base, head string, modules []validationModule\n \t\tgitArgs = append(gitArgs, head)\n \t}\n \tgitArgs = append(gitArgs, \"--\")\n-\tout, err := posemodel.RawGit(gitArgs...).Output()\n+\t// The diff reads the index without writing it (spec\n+\t// pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1).\n+\tout, err := posemodel.RawGitDiffReadOnly(root, gitArgs...)\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn sel, fmt.Errorf(\"git diff %s failed (revision unknown?)\", sel.rangeLabel())\n \t}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go\nindex b95cd8fb..e0bc034f 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go\n@@ -656,7 +656,10 @@ func gitCommandContext(ctx context.Context, args ...string) *exec.Cmd {\n \t\t\tenv = append(env, kv)\n \t\t}\n \t}\n-\tcmd.Env = append(env, \"GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS=1\", \"GIT_GRAFT_FILE=\"+os.DevNull)\n+\t// An engine read never takes the optional index lock nor rewrites the\n+\t// index's stat cache: a concurrent reader would see .git change under\n+\t// it (spec pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1).\n+\tcmd.Env = append(env, \"GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS=1\", \"GIT_GRAFT_FILE=\"+os.DevNull, \"GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0\")\n \treturn cmd\n }\n \ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..a9dbd243\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@\n+package pose\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"fmt\"\n+\t\"os/exec\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+)\n+\n+// Spec pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1, D1: `git diff` against\n+// the work tree refreshes the index's stat cache and writes it back even with\n+// GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0, and diff.autoRefreshIndex=false would change its\n+// answer (a file whose stat alone changed would be listed). So the diff runs\n+// as it is, but reads the index through a descriptor whose lock Git cannot\n+// create: it refreshes in memory, cannot write, and skips the write silently\n+// (refresh_index_quietly), so its answer is the plain diff's and nothing is\n+// written anywhere. Where that is not available, it reads a private copy.\n+\n+// diffIndexLimit bounds the index one read loads.\n+const diffIndexLimit = 512 << 20\n+\n+// ReadOnlyIndex prepares cmd, a git command reading the repository at root,\n+// to read root's index without being able to write it. The returned function\n+// releases what it holds; call it after the command ends.\n+func ReadOnlyIndex(cmd *exec.Cmd, root string) (func(), error) {\n+\tout, err := RawGit(\"-C\", root, \"rev-parse\", \"--path-format=absolute\", \"--git-path\", \"index\").Output()\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s cannot be located: %w\", root, err)\n+\t}\n+\traw, err := readBoundedRegular(strings.TrimSuffix(string(out), \"\\n\"), diffIndexLimit)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s cannot be read: %w\", root, err)\n+\t}\n+\treturn readOnlyIndexFor(cmd, raw)\n+}\n+\n+// RawGitDiffReadOnly runs RawGit(args...), a diff of the repository at root,\n+// reading its index without writing it, and returns its standard output.\n+func RawGitDiffReadOnly(root string, args ...string) ([]byte, error) {\n+\tcmd := RawGit(args...)\n+\tdone, err := ReadOnlyIndex(cmd, root)\n+\tdefer done()\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn nil, err\n+\t}\n+\treturn cmd.Output()\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..05ef93ed\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@\n+//go:build linux\n+\n+package pose\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"fmt\"\n+\t\"os\"\n+\t\"os/exec\"\n+\n+\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n+)\n+\n+// readOnlyIndexFor hands raw to cmd as an anonymous memory file. Git\n+// resolves the link /proc/self/fd/N to \"/memfd:pose-index/none (deleted)\"\n+// and tries to create its lock next to it, in a directory that does not\n+// exist, so the lock fails for any user, root included, and the refresh is\n+// not written. No file is created.\n+func readOnlyIndexFor(cmd *exec.Cmd, raw []byte) (func(), error) {\n+\tfd, err := unix.MemfdCreate(\"pose-index/none\", unix.MFD_CLOEXEC)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: an in-memory index cannot be made: %w\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tf := os.NewFile(uintptr(fd), \"pose-index\")\n+\tif _, err := f.Write(raw); err != nil {\n+\t\tf.Close()\n+\t\treturn func() {}, err\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := f.Seek(0, 0); err != nil {\n+\t\tf.Close()\n+\t\treturn func() {}, err\n+\t}\n+\tcmd.ExtraFiles = append(cmd.ExtraFiles, f)\n+\tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Env, fmt.Sprintf(\"GIT_INDEX_FILE=/proc/self/fd/%d\", 2+len(cmd.ExtraFiles)))\n+\treturn func() { f.Close() }, nil\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_other.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_other.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..1b633784\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_other.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@\n+//go:build !linux\n+\n+package pose\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"os\"\n+\t\"os/exec\"\n+\t\"path/filepath\"\n+)\n+\n+// readOnlyIndexFor hands raw to cmd as a private copy: Git refreshes and may\n+// rewrite the copy, never the checkout's index.\n+func readOnlyIndexFor(cmd *exec.Cmd, raw []byte) (func(), error) {\n+\tdir, err := os.MkdirTemp(\"\", \"pose-index-*\")\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn func() {}, err\n+\t}\n+\tdone := func() { _ = os.RemoveAll(dir) }\n+\tpath := filepath.Join(dir, \"index\")\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(path, raw, 0o600); err != nil {\n+\t\tdone()\n+\t\treturn func() {}, err\n+\t}\n+\t// A split index would write a new shared index into .git.\n+\tcmd.Args = append([]string{cmd.Args[0], \"-c\", \"core.splitIndex=false\"}, cmd.Args[1:]...)\n+\tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Env, \"GIT_INDEX_FILE=\"+path)\n+\treturn done, nil\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..fbe9c788\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,142 @@\n+package pose\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"bytes\"\n+\t\"os\"\n+\t\"os/exec\"\n+\t\"path/filepath\"\n+\t\"testing\"\n+\t\"time\"\n+)\n+\n+// Spec pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1, R2: a diff that reads the\n+// index read-only answers exactly as the plain diff does, over the states\n+// review round 1 found a status-based reading got wrong, and leaves the index\n+// byte-identical where the plain diff rewrites it.\n+func TestReadOnlyIndexDiffAnswersAsThePlainDiff(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot := t.TempDir()\n+\trun := func(dir string, args ...string) string {\n+\t\tt.Helper()\n+\t\tcmd := exec.Command(\"git\", append([]string{\"-C\", dir, \"-c\", \"user.name=t\", \"-c\", \"user.email=t@t\", \"-c\", \"protocol.file.allow=always\"}, args...)...)\n+\t\tout, err := cmd.CombinedOutput()\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"git %v: %v %s\", args, err, out)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\treturn string(out)\n+\t}\n+\twrite := func(rel, body string) {\n+\t\tt.Helper()\n+\t\tp := filepath.Join(root, rel)\n+\t\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(p), 0o755); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(p, []byte(body), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\t// A submodule whose .gitmodules says ignore=all.\n+\tsub := t.TempDir()\n+\trun(sub, \"init\", \"-q\")\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(sub, \"s.txt\"), []byte(\"1\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\trun(sub, \"add\", \"s.txt\")\n+\trun(sub, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"s1\")\n+\trun(root, \"init\", \"-q\")\n+\tfor _, f := range []string{\"stat.txt\", \"mod.txt\", \"del.txt\", \"proj/back.txt\", \"dir/x.txt\", \"conflict.txt\"} {\n+\t\twrite(f, \"x\\n\")\n+\t}\n+\tif err := os.Symlink(\"target-missing\", filepath.Join(root, \"link\")); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\trun(root, \"add\", \"-A\")\n+\trun(root, \"submodule\", \"add\", \"-q\", sub, \"mod\")\n+\trun(root, \"config\", \"-f\", \".gitmodules\", \"submodule.mod.ignore\", \"all\")\n+\trun(root, \"add\", \".gitmodules\")\n+\trun(root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"base\")\n+\tbase := run(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\")[:40]\n+\t// A commit since the base: the gitlink moves, and a file changes and is\n+\t// changed back in the work tree.\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, \"mod\", \"s.txt\"), []byte(\"2\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\trun(filepath.Join(root, \"mod\"), \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-am\", \"s2\")\n+\twrite(\"proj/back.txt\", \"y\\n\")\n+\trun(root, \"add\", \"-A\")\n+\trun(root, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"next\")\n+\twrite(\"proj/back.txt\", \"x\\n\")\n+\t// Work-tree states.\n+\twrite(\"mod.txt\", \"changed\\n\")\n+\tif err := os.Remove(filepath.Join(root, \"del.txt\")); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\twrite(\"staged.txt\", \"s\\n\")\n+\trun(root, \"add\", \"staged.txt\")\n+\twrite(\"ita.txt\", \"i\\n\")\n+\trun(root, \"add\", \"-N\", \"ita.txt\")\n+\twrite(\"conflict.txt\", \"staged then reverted\\n\")\n+\trun(root, \"add\", \"conflict.txt\")\n+\twrite(\"conflict.txt\", \"x\\n\")\n+\tif err := os.RemoveAll(filepath.Join(root, \"dir\")); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\twrite(\"dir\", \"now a file\\n\")\n+\tlater := time.Now().Add(2 * time.Second)\n+\tif err := os.Chtimes(filepath.Join(root, \"stat.txt\"), later, later); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\treads := [][]string{\n+\t\t{\"-C\", root, \"-c\", \"diff.ignoreSubmodules=none\", \"diff\", \"--ignore-submodules=none\", \"--name-only\", \"-z\", \"--no-renames\", base, \"--\"},\n+\t\t{\"-C\", root, \"diff\", \"HEAD\", \"--name-status\", \"--no-renames\", \"--diff-filter=MDT\", \"--\"},\n+\t\t{\"-C\", filepath.Join(root, \"proj\"), \"diff\", \"--name-only\", base},\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, args := range reads {\n+\t\tbefore, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\"))\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tgot, err := RawGitDiffReadOnly(root, args...)\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%v: %v\", args, err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tafter, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\"))\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif !bytes.Equal(before, after) {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%v rewrote .git/index\", args)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\twant, err := RawGit(args...).Output()\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif !bytes.Equal(got, want) {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%v answered %q, the plain diff %q\", args, got, want)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\t// Make the stat cache stale again for the next read.\n+\t\tlater = later.Add(2 * time.Second)\n+\t\tif err := os.Chtimes(filepath.Join(root, \"stat.txt\"), later, later); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\t// The review history ledger's own diff (review round 1, N9).\n+\tbefore, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\"))\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := reviewHistoryGit(root, \"diff\", \"HEAD\", \"--name-status\", \"--no-renames\", \"--diff-filter=MDT\", \"--\"); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tif after, _ := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\")); !bytes.Equal(before, after) {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"the review history diff rewrote .git/index\")\n+\t}\n+\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(filepath.Join(root, \".git\"))\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, e := range entries {\n+\t\tif filepath.Ext(e.Name()) == \".lock\" {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a read left %s\", e.Name())\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\nindex 8cd9edb4..15a1dae2 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n@@ -530,6 +530,15 @@ func reviewHistoryGit(root string, args ...string) ([]byte, error) {\n \tbase := gitCommand(append([]string{\"-C\", root}, args...)...)\n \tcmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, \"git\", base.Args[1:]...)\n \tcmd.Env = base.Env\n+\tif len(args) > 0 && args[0] == \"diff\" {\n+\t\t// A diff against the work tree reads the index without writing it\n+\t\t// (spec pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1).\n+\t\tdone, err := ReadOnlyIndex(cmd, root)\n+\t\tdefer done()\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"review history Git observation unavailable: %w\", err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n \tvar out reviewHistoryBuffer\n \tcmd.Stdout = &out\n \tif err := cmd.Run(); err != nil {","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WuwumZBuZ3JCxRwPabg2fC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
